    "result_text": "All green. The full suite builds and passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `Owner` entity gained an optional `registrationDate`; when a POST omits it, the server's current date is used, and the value round-trips as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, mirroring how `PetFields.birthDate` is defined. It's optional (not in `required`), so it appears on both the request DTO and the response `OwnerDto`, and MapStruct maps it automatically by name in both directions.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field with `@Column(name = \"registration_date\", columnDefinition = \"DATE\")`, getter/setter, and a `toString` entry.\n\n3. **`DefaultRegistrationDate.java`** (new) \u2014 a single-responsibility OfficeFloor step: if the built owner has no registration date, set it to `LocalDate.now()`. `@Val` yields the stored `Owner`, so it mutates in place and later steps (save/respond) see it.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n5. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2 active, plus hsqldb/postgres/mysql for consistency).\n\nDesign notes: defaulting lives in its own step rather than being bolted onto `BuildOwner` (which only maps DTO\u2192entity) \u2014 keeping each unit focused. `ApplyOwner` (the PUT path) was intentionally left untouched, so updates preserve an existing registration date rather than overwriting it. Jackson serializes `LocalDate` from a `format: date` field as `YYYY-MM-DD` with no extra config.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (`coreDefaultsToToday`, `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) and the full suite pass \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
